# The packet filter of the network share, for iptables-legacy-restore.
# S45neptron-share loads it before it starts the SMB server and mDNS, and
# starts neither when the load fails.
#
# The share is open to guests, read-write, so only clients on the local
# network may reach it: loopback, the private IPv4 ranges of RFC 1918, and
# the link-local range. Any other source, such as a host on the internet
# when the PC has a public address, gets no answer on TCP 445 (SMB) and
# UDP 5353 (mDNS). ksmbd-tools 3.5.2 has no address limit of its own:
# "hosts allow" compares the client address as an exact string, with no
# range or mask. The images have no IPv6, so no IPv6 rule is needed.
#
# board/common/check-share-filter.sh fails the build when the rule lines
# of this file are not exactly these.
*filter
:INPUT ACCEPT [0:0]
:FORWARD ACCEPT [0:0]
:OUTPUT ACCEPT [0:0]
:neptron-lan - [0:0]
-A INPUT -p tcp -m tcp --dport 445 -j neptron-lan
-A INPUT -p udp -m udp --dport 5353 -j neptron-lan
-A neptron-lan -s 127.0.0.0/8 -j ACCEPT
-A neptron-lan -s 10.0.0.0/8 -j ACCEPT
-A neptron-lan -s 172.16.0.0/12 -j ACCEPT
-A neptron-lan -s 192.168.0.0/16 -j ACCEPT
-A neptron-lan -s 169.254.0.0/16 -j ACCEPT
-A neptron-lan -j DROP
COMMIT
